                <pb facs="0671" n="591" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg591"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51W89 Italy/281: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Long</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-02-27T12:00:00-05:00">February 27,
                            1936—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>17. Reference your letter January 31 to the President regarding acquisition of
                    residence as part of settlement of debt which in principle has our unqualified
                    approval.</p>
                <p>Will you therefore in your discretion take such steps as may be necessary to find
                    out definitely whether a settlement can be arranged and the residence offered as
                    part payment. If a reasonably satisfactory offer is forthcoming along the lines
                    of your letter of January 31, I will be glad to consult our leaders in Congress,
                    since payment in this way necessitates congressional authorization. Please cable
                    developments.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
